Sval: media devices the page hasn't been granted keep a constant list

A new RFPTarget, MediaDevicesBeforePermission, gives enumerateDevices
RFPTarget::MediaDevices' shape (one device, faked where the machine has
none) for each input kind whose info the page can't see, as
MediaDevices::CanExposeInfo answers it.
A camera grant shows the real cameras and nothing about microphones; a
microphone grant shows the real microphones and nothing about cameras.
Speakers keep Gecko's own rules, which follow the microphone grant. It
reuses MediaDevices' code in MediaDevices::FilterExposedDevices; the rest of
the MediaDevices target (unpersisted device ids, reduced constraints,
"Always Ask" read as prompt) stays with that target, because after a grant
the user has consented to that kind's real list.

No chrome API can change what enumerateDevices reports.

diff --git a/dom/media/MediaDevices.cpp b/dom/media/MediaDevices.cpp
index 5c4939eca5..3c3f2c97b5 100644
--- a/dom/media/MediaDevices.cpp
+++ b/dom/media/MediaDevices.cpp
@@ -343,14 +343,23 @@ RefPtr<MediaDeviceSetRefCnt> MediaDevices::FilterExposedDevices(
     exposed->AppendElement(device);
   }
 
-  if (doc->ShouldResistFingerprinting(RFPTarget::MediaDevices)) {
+  // MediaDevicesBeforePermission gives the same shape to each kind whose info
+  // the page can't see yet; a granted kind, and the speakers that follow the
+  // microphone grant, keep the list Gecko exposes.
+  const bool shapeAll =
+      doc->ShouldResistFingerprinting(RFPTarget::MediaDevices);
+  const auto shaped = [&](MediaDeviceKind aKind) {
+    return shapeAll || !CanExposeInfo(aKind);
+  };
+  if (shapeAll || doc->ShouldResistFingerprinting(
+                      RFPTarget::MediaDevicesBeforePermission)) {
     // We expose a single device of each kind.
     // Legacy mode also achieves the same thing, except for speakers.
     nsTHashSet<MediaDeviceKind> seenKinds;
 
     for (uint32_t i = 0; i < exposed->Length(); i++) {
       RefPtr<mozilla::MediaDevice> device = exposed->ElementAt(i);
-      if (seenKinds.Contains(device->mKind)) {
+      if (seenKinds.Contains(device->mKind) && shaped(device->mKind)) {
         exposed->RemoveElementAt(i);
         i--;
         continue;
@@ -367,20 +376,30 @@ RefPtr<MediaDeviceSetRefCnt> MediaDevices::FilterExposedDevices(
       // The order in which we insert the fake devices is important.
       // Microphone is inserted first, then camera, then speaker.
       // If we haven't seen a microphone, insert a fake one.
-      if (!seenKinds.Contains(MediaDeviceKind::Audioinput)) {
